-# Prompt Architect
-
-Replaces pi's default main system-prompt block with a sectioned skeleton, gated
-on the tools that are actually active, and deduplicates the prompt sources pi
-injects around it.
-
-Modelled on how [omp (oh-my-pi)](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi) organizes
-its prompt — capability-gated template sections, source-level deduplication, a
-separate delivery contract — while keeping pi's own mechanism (ordered named
-sections with diff patching) and leaving `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`
-untouched, so nothing breaks on upgrade.
-
-## What it changes
-
-The composed main block is rendered into `systemPromptOptions.customPrompt`.
-pi keeps rendering the footer after it, so context files, skills, and cwd are
-still handled by pi itself.
-
-```
-[composed main block]
-  <role>                persona and engineering taste
-  <tools>               one line per active tool, no filler
-  <rules>               merged tool + extension guidelines, deduplicated
-  <docs>                condensed pointer to pi's own documentation
-  <tool_policy>         capability-gated MCP, delegation, plugin, and specialized-tool routing
-  <workflow>            scope → research → decompose → implement → verify → cleanup
-  <delivery_contract>   completion, evidence, and blocking contract
-[pi footer, unchanged]
-  <addendum> <project_context> <skills> <cwd>
-```
-
-Two behaviours are worth calling out:
-
-- **Capability gating.** Routing for model-callable plugins is rendered only
-  when its tool is active. `subagents_enable` enables delegation, `subagent`
-  launches it, and `subagent_supervisor` only replies to child requests. MCP
-  service hints are rendered only when `mcp` is active. User-side `/usage`,
-  `/rewind`, and `/open-tui` are identified as commands, not model tools.
-- **Deduplication.** When a project `AGENTS.md` restates a global one in full,
-  the global copy is dropped as a whole file. Matching is exact
-  paragraph-subsequence containment, never fuzzy, so a paraphrased rule always
-  survives. Partially overlapping files are both kept.
-
-The extension **stands down** when `customPrompt` is already set — that is, when
-you placed a `SYSTEM.md` or passed `--system-prompt`. Your explicit prompt wins;
-only deduplication still runs.
-
-Any error inside the handler leaves pi's options untouched and writes one line
-to stderr, so this extension can never block a session.
-
-## Layout
-
-```
-index.ts               pi extension: before_agent_start + /prompt-audit + /prompt-export
-composer.mjs           pure composer — no pi imports, runs under plain node
-dedupe.mjs             paragraph-containment deduplication
-fragments/*.md         the prose sections, one file per block
-scripts/               tooling (not loaded by pi: the directory scan is one level deep)
-```
-
-## Commands
-
-```sh
-cd ~/.pi/agent/extensions/prompt-architect
-
-node scripts/check-prompts.mjs          # report unformatted fragments, exit 1 if any
-node scripts/check-prompts.mjs --fix    # rewrite them in place
-node scripts/measure-prompt.mjs         # token accounting vs pi's default block
-node scripts/measure-prompt.mjs --print # print the composed main block
+# Prompt Architect — Pi 1.0
+
+Adds four independent policy sections using `systemPromptOptions.sections`:
+`engineering`, `tool_policy`, `workflow`, `delivery_contract`.
+Pi owns its native preamble, tools, rules, docs, addendum, context, skills,
+cwd, MCP server instructions and Code mode. This extension never copies the
+native prompt renderer or assigns `customPrompt`.
+
+Policies are capability-gated on the active tools at run start. Pi's native
+renderer remains responsible for declarations and guidelines when tools are
+activated later. Subsequent plugins can add guidelines or their own sections
+without losing them. Code mode instructions use native `searchTools()` and
+`describeNamespace()`; obsolete `mcp` / `mcpScript` gateway instructions are removed.
+Desktop observation/input tools are model-only, preserving their image context.
+
+An explicit `forceSystemPrompt` (including an empty value) is opaque: no options
+are changed. An existing `customPrompt` from SYSTEM.md / CLI keeps ownership;
+no engineering policies are added. Complete duplicate context sources are
+deduplicated using exact paragraph containment; partial overlaps and paraphrases
+stay intact. A fragment load failure logs an error without blocking the session.
+
+## Organization
+
+- `index.ts`: Pi hooks and `/prompt-audit`, `/prompt-export <new-file>` commands.
+- `composer.mjs`: pure deterministic policy composition, no runtime SDK import.
+- `fragments/`: engineering discipline, active-tool routing, workflow, delivery.
+- `dedupe.mjs`: exact complete-source deduplication, fenced examples preserved.
+- `scripts/measure-prompt.mjs`: additive size estimate and capability self-test.
+- `scripts/smoke-test.mjs`: extension-hook ownership checks.
+
+```powershell
 node scripts/measure-prompt.mjs --selftest
-node scripts/smoke-test.mjs             # load index.ts through jiti with a stubbed pi
+node scripts/smoke-test.mjs
 ```
 
-`/prompt-audit` inside a pi session reports the per-block estimate, the active
-tool set, and any context files that were dropped. Use `/prompt-export ./full-prompt.txt`
-to write the **last agent run's full effective system prompt** (including Pi's
-footer) to a new file in the current directory. The command does not overwrite existing
-files. The `--print` script only prints the composed main block, not the full
-prompt. After `/reload`, send a normal message first so `before_agent_start`
-applies the new prompt, then run `/prompt-export ./full-prompt.txt`. Exporting
-before the first model turn would capture Pi's initial prompt instead. Review
-the export before sharing it; it may contain private context.
-
-## Token accounting
-
-pi does not export a tokenizer, so every count here is `ceil(utf8 bytes / 4)` —
-an estimate, not a measurement.
-
-The exact numbers depend on active tools and plugin guidelines. Run
-`node scripts/measure-prompt.mjs` for the fixture comparison or `/prompt-audit`
-in a live session. `<rules>` includes third-party extensions' own guidelines;
-the composer preserves them and adds short call-routing hints.
-
-The point of the measurement script is not a smaller prompt — it is a **bounded**
-one. `MAX_OVERHEAD_EST_TOKENS` in `measure-prompt.mjs` caps how much the
-discipline sections may add on a fixed fixture tool set, and `--selftest` fails
-when that cap is exceeded, so the prompt cannot quietly drift upward. The
-fixture is a regression guard, not an exact tokenizer or live-session measure.
-
-## Notes
-
-- `composer.mjs` must stay deterministic. No `Date`, no `Math.random`, no
-  unordered iteration — a varying main block would emit a fresh system-prompt
-  patch on every turn and defeat prompt caching.
-- Gate a line by putting it in a data table in `composer.mjs` and rendering it
-  only when its tool is active. Put prose in `fragments/*.md`. Do not add a
-  template language.
-- Removing the extension is enough to revert: delete the directory and restart.
+Token counts are UTF-8 bytes / 4 estimates, not model tokenizer results. `/prompt-export`
+exports the last active run's effective prompt and refuses to overwrite a file.
+Full prompt exports can contain private project context; review before sharing.
+The provider-facing SDK audit lives in pi-orb `evidence/upgrade-0.10/run-prompt-audit.mjs`.
